  "provenance": {
    "label": "synthetic generated aerial-human REMOTE-AWARE hard trade-off mission diagnostic (second world img_2)",
    "assets": "OpenAI-generated synthetic humans (owner-supplied); NOT real people, NOT real aerial data",
    "note": "results are integration/observability diagnostics, never real UAV, radio, or Jetson performance",
    "design": "V2.4 hard trade-off structure with a live remote/network/privacy axis: small early targets (~32 px, validated Stage B) defeat the light model; large late targets sit in ~1.5 s windows on odd capture times so the strong executor's configured 1.4 s latency skips them; the network starts on a good link (remote inference viable) and degrades mid-mission; the communication budget is sized so an always-remote policy breaches it while an adaptive policy's affordability rule stops in time; energy_j_per_call for the strong config and uplink_energy_j_per_mb for the radio are stress-configured (simulated, modelling a power-hungry accelerator and a long-range high-power link) so always-strong breaches the battery floor and the remote phase still consumes mission-relevant battery",
    "network": "named regimes are CONFIGURED simulation parameters, not radio measurements",
    "remote": "simulated_remote runs the strong torchvision strategy in-process behind the deployment transport boundary; latency is DERIVED from the capture-time network snapshot (Model A) plus configured stage components; communication energy is CONFIGURED J/MB",
    "latency_energy": "mission_latency_s and energy_j_per_call are CONFIGURED/SIMULATED for deterministic, machine-independent missions; measured wall-clock is recorded as a diagnostic only",
